<p>The Benagil Cave, also known as the "Cathedral" due to its impressive size and shape, was formed over thousands of years by the relentless action of the sea on the limestone cliffs. The cave features a large opening to the sea and a spectacular natural skylight in its roof, allowing sunlight to flood the interior and create a magical atmosphere with ever-changing light patterns reflecting on the turquoise water.</p>
